Uniform signed-module runtime and targeted originals, 2026-09-28
===============================================================

Scope: the completed 7,002-target-C composition, not a new full 970-program
campaign and not the separately configured expanded KUnit population.

Both sides install all 847 linked kernel modules through the original
Makefile.modinst signing/install path. Each installed object is checked against
its exact linked body plus signature trailer; depmod completes and the protected
Image/config/vmlinux/target-object hashes remain unchanged. CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_ALL
is enabled, but CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE is not: successful loading alone is NOT
proof that rejection of an untrusted signature was enforced.

The 17 BPF/livepatch support modules are rebuilt against their respective kernel
build trees from all 22 unchanged original sources. These are reference-built
test infrastructure, not EvoCC-compiled target-C credit. All 4,393 original
non-module regular test files retain identical bytes. The original OVPN helper
inputs and variant aliases are supplied; common prerequisite loads include
fuse, snd_timer, ntsync and virtual_ncidev. Per-flight disks use QEMU snapshots.

New ext4 disks: reference 4.25 GiB logical / about 3.1 GiB allocated;
subject 5.25 GiB logical / about 3.9 GiB allocated. e2fsck -fn is clean for both.
The approximately 4 GiB extraction/staging tree was deleted only after checking
no open handles; it can be recreated from the retained disk. No workspace,
kernel source clone, historical receipt or original test is deleted.

Actual common-runner execution, original argv/budgets, six selected programs:
  program                         GCC                      EvoCC
  bpf:test_kmod.sh                 TIMEOUT 300s             TIMEOUT 300s
  fpu:run_test_fpu.sh              SKIP                     SKIP
  iommu:iommufd                   PASS (224/0/5 inner)     PASS (224/0/5 inner)
  nci:nci_dev                     PASS (8/8 inner)         PASS (8/8 inner)
  splice:default_file_splice_read.sh PASS                    PASS
  splice:short_splice_read.sh       PASS                    PASS
All twelve nonce-bound boots and orderly shutdowns PASS. The original inventory
still contains 970 programs; the other 964 are NOT_RUN on each side. The receipt
is correctly INCOMPLETE. The first two module probes do not promote all 847
installed modules to runtime-tested status. The earlier September 22 full-run
totals remain in that historical summary.

FPU's actual script explicitly reports CONFIG_TEST_FPU=m missing; this is NOT
a PASS. The frozen fpu collection has no config fragment. lib/Kconfig.debug
requires ARCH_HAS_KERNEL_FPU_SUPPORT and !KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL. The current
configuration already has architecture support and no KCOV, but TEST_FPU=n.
The common source-pinned prerequisite review now lists this missing module and
its dependencies. Its new test is RED before repair, GREEN afterwards; all
271 K1 Python tests, targeted Ruff and diff whitespace checks PASS. Changed
source invalidates the review; no configuration or original verdict is rewritten.
Enabled FPU module build/install/runtime is still K12f, not closed by the audit.

